    "highlights": [
      "Natural gas is cheap in Michigan ($1.03 per therm, the 9th lowest of 51), so a gas tank costs only about $187 a year to run, and gas stays the cheapest tank to own over 10 years.",
      "66% of Michigan homes heat water with natural gas, against 48% nationally, so most replacements here are gas-to-gas with an existing vent and gas line.",
      "Incoming water drops to about 41.2 °F in the coldest month, so a whole-house tankless unit manages only one full-flow shower at a time in winter; a tank, or two tankless units, suits larger households better.",
      "Where you live inside Michigan matters: the same 50-gallon gas job is about $1,817 in the Ann Arbor, MI area and $1,746 in the Flint, MI area."
    ]
